  "question": {
    "text": "The rate of a chemical reaction doubles for every $10^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ rise of temperature. If the temperature is raised by $50^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$, the rate of the reaction increases by about :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n24 times\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n32 times\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n64 times\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n10 times",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Temperature coefficient $\\mu=2$;\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mu^{\\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{T}}{10}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1} \\\\\n& 2^{\\frac{50}{10}}=2^5=32=\\frac{\\mathrm{k}_2}{\\mathrm{k}_1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nTherefore $32 \\mathrm{k}_1=\\mathrm{k}_2$"
  }
}